  "question": {
    "text": "A metal rod of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> has cross-sectional areas <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>A</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> as shown in the figure. The ends are maintained at temperatures <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>70</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>. The temperature at middle point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>&nbsp;(in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>°</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>) is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/Q_33.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 131px;\" />",
    "image": null
